# 📌 Vulnerability Report: URI-Based Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)

---

# 🎯 Objective

Identify and validate security vulnerabilities within the target application's subdomains through reconnaissance and parameter testing.

---

# 📖 Description

During security testing of a private bug bounty program, a potentially vulnerable redirect endpoint was discovered through Google Dorking. The endpoint accepted user-controlled input through a `redirect` parameter.

Further testing revealed that the application failed to properly validate URI schemes supplied to the parameter. As a result, an attacker could inject a malicious `javascript:` URI, leading to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS).

The vulnerable endpoint was identified as:

```http
https://example.com/social?redirect=/somewhere
```

---

# 🎯 Affected Component

| Component          | Details                       |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------- |
| Feature            | Social Redirect Functionality |
| Parameter          | redirect                      |
| Vulnerability Type | Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)    |
| Discovery Method   | Google Dorking                |
| Scope              | Multiple program domains      |

---

# 🔍 Root Cause

The application failed to properly validate and restrict URI schemes passed to the `redirect` parameter.

Instead of allowing only trusted protocols such as:

```text
https://
http://
```

the application also accepted:

```text
javascript:
```

This resulted in arbitrary JavaScript execution within the victim's browser.

---

# ⚠️ Impact

Successful exploitation could allow an attacker to:

* Execute arbitrary JavaScript in the victim's browser.
* Perform phishing attacks.
* Capture user keystrokes.
* Steal non-HttpOnly session tokens.
* Modify page content.
* Perform actions on behalf of authenticated users.
* Increase attack effectiveness by combining logout and login redirection.

---

# 🛠️ Technical Details

## Reconnaissance

Google Dorking was performed against the program's assets.

### Search Query

```text
site:*.example.com inurl:redirect
```

Additional keywords tested:

```text
admin
url
redirect
next
redirect_to
page
site
```

---

## Endpoint Discovery

A redirect endpoint was identified:

```http
https://example.com/social?redirect=/somewhere
```

---

## Open Redirect Verification

The redirect parameter was tested with an external URL.

### Payload

```http
https://example.com/social?redirect=https://google.com
```

### Result

The application successfully redirected users to an external domain, confirming an Open Redirect.

