# 🏁 Conclusion

A URI-based Cross-Site Scripting vulnerability was identified through Google Dorking and parameter analysis. The root cause was insufficient validation of the `redirect` parameter, allowing execution of malicious `javascript:` URIs. The issue affected multiple domains within the program scope and could lead to phishing, account compromise, and client-side code execution.
